meta {
  name: Import Steam Library (Stream)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{backendUrl}}/api/user/steam/import/stream
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

docs {
  SSE variant of "Import Steam Library" (media_type: text/event-stream),
  same event shape and caveat as "Sync Steam Playtimes (Stream)" -
  Bruno's plain HTTP request type will just return the raw
  event-stream body once the connection closes, not live progress. Run
  auth/Login and user/Set Steam ID first.

  The body is optional: without one (or with null) every unlinked owned
  game is imported; with a JSON array like [{"appid": 620}] the import
  is restricted to those app ids - the preview-before-import flow on the
  Steam page sends exactly the app ids the user confirmed in the
  preview, so the import always matches it.

  503 if neither the caller nor the server has a Steam Web API key
  configured - this is a real top-level HTTP response, raised before
  the SSE stream opens. A missing Steam ID, by contrast, surfaces as an
  `error` event inside an HTTP 200 stream, not as a 400. An appid below
  1 or a list over 10000 items is a plain 400 before the stream opens.
}
